From 08030fdbe4432834126b3cc3bbcdc34054fe5417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 16:03:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PhoneWindowManager: bind the spare Mapper button to a
 display-freeze recovery
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The mini-HDMI mirror can wedge the vendor composer so that it stops delivering
vsync while still reporting it as enabled: SurfaceFlinger then composes nothing
and both displays freeze with the hardware still scanning out. A screen off/on
cycle is the only reliable recovery. It cannot be an on-screen action, because
the display is frozen at that point and the user cannot see what they would be
tapping — but input still reaches the framework, so a hardware key works.

The GPD XD+'s "Gamepad Mapper" button (kernel scancode 88) is already mapped to
the otherwise unused F12 in mtk-kpd.kl as a neutral interception anchor, so
nothing has to be suppressed. Off by default; the GPD XD+ settings screen arms it
via persist.sys.xdplus.hdmi_recovery_key, which is read per press.

Verified: with the toggle off, or with no HDMI cable attached, the key does
nothing at all. When armed with a cable present, one press logs "Going to sleep
due to power_button" then "Waking up ... XDPLUS_RECOVERY" 700 ms later, and a
frozen mirror session goes from zero display triggers back to 36-44 posts/s.
Confirmed on the physical button, not just an injected keycode. The bounce
revives the panel only, so the bring-up is re-dispatched afterwards to bring the
mirror back as well (that half is not yet verified end to end: HDMI bring-up
itself still crashes system_server on some boots, which is a separate defect).

Changes:
- Intercept `KEYCODE_F12` in `interceptKeyBeforeQueueing()`: on the initial down, when armed, consume the event, sleep the display and wake it again after `XDPLUS_RECOVERY_WAKE_DELAY_MS` (700 ms, so the composer actually tears down in between rather than the wake racing the sleep)
- Gate on `isXdplusHdmiCablePresent()` reading the extcon switch, so the button is a no-op with nothing plugged in and cannot sleep the device on a stray press; the check fails OPEN, because losing the only recovery from a frozen screen is worse than an occasional stray bounce
- Re-dispatch the mirror bring-up `XDPLUS_RECOVERY_HDMI_UP_DELAY_MS` (3 s) after the wake via the existing `sys.xdplus.action=hdmi_up` init hook, since the bounce alone leaves the external session dormant

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I44b5baf4e0c90de515164c655852ccf159e68603
---
 .../server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java     | 76 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 76 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
index 28724e2e..1c40c8d0 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/policy/PhoneWindowManager.java
@@ -307,6 +307,14 @@ public class PhoneWindowManager implements WindowManagerPolicy {
     static final int DOUBLE_TAP_HOME_NOTHING = 0;
     static final int DOUBLE_TAP_HOME_RECENT_SYSTEM_UI = 1;
 
+    // GPD XD+ (§104): delay between the sleep and the wake of the spare-button
+    // display-freeze recovery, so the composer actually tears down in between.
+    static final long XDPLUS_RECOVERY_WAKE_DELAY_MS = 700;
+    // GPD XD+ (§105): the bounce revives the panel but not the mirror, so the
+    // bring-up is re-dispatched afterwards — late enough for the framework to have
+    // settled after the wake.
+    static final long XDPLUS_RECOVERY_HDMI_UP_DELAY_MS = 3000;
+
     static final int SHORT_PRESS_WINDOW_NOTHING = 0;
     static final int SHORT_PRESS_WINDOW_PICTURE_IN_PICTURE = 1;
 
@@ -4583,6 +4591,52 @@ public class PhoneWindowManager implements WindowManagerPolicy {
                 break;
             }
 
+            case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_F12: {
+                // GPD XD+ (§104): display-freeze recovery on the spare "Gamepad
+                // Mapper" hardware button (kernel scancode 88, mapped to the
+                // otherwise unused F12 in mtk-kpd.kl).
+                //
+                // The mini-HDMI mirror can wedge the vendor composer so that it
+                // stops delivering vsync while still reporting it enabled: SF then
+                // composes nothing and BOTH displays freeze with the hardware
+                // still scanning out. A screen off/on cycle is the only reliable
+                // recovery, and it cannot be offered in the UI — the screen is
+                // frozen, so the user cannot see what they would be tapping. Input
+                // still reaches the framework in that state, so a hardware key is
+                // the only workable trigger.
+                //
+                // Off by default; the GPD XD+ settings screen arms it.
+                if (down && event.getRepeatCount() == 0
+                        && SystemProperties.getBoolean(
+                                "persist.sys.xdplus.hdmi_recovery_key", false)
+                        && isXdplusHdmiCablePresent()) {
+                    result &= ~ACTION_PASS_TO_USER;
+                    isWakeKey = false;
+                    Slog.i(TAG, "XD+ recovery key: bouncing the display off/on");
+                    goToSleep(event.getEventTime(), PowerManager.GO_TO_SLEEP_REASON_POWER_BUTTON,
+                            0);
+                    // Give the display and the composer time to tear down before
+                    // waking, otherwise the wake races the sleep and the composer
+                    // keeps its wedged state.
+                    mHandler.postDelayed(
+                            () -> wakeUp(SystemClock.uptimeMillis(),
+                                    mAllowTheaterModeWakeFromPowerKey,
+                                    PowerManager.WAKE_REASON_POWER_BUTTON,
+                                    "android.policy:XDPLUS_RECOVERY"),
+                            XDPLUS_RECOVERY_WAKE_DELAY_MS);
+                    // The bounce revives the built-in panel but leaves the
+                    // external session dormant, so the mirror has to be brought
+                    // up again — re-run the bring-up through the existing init
+                    // dispatch (init.xdplus.rc: on property:sys.xdplus.action).
+                    // Delayed well past the wake so the framework has settled
+                    // before hdmictl starts poking the display path.
+                    mHandler.postDelayed(
+                            () -> SystemProperties.set("sys.xdplus.action", "hdmi_up"),
+                            XDPLUS_RECOVERY_HDMI_UP_DELAY_MS);
+                }
+                break;
+            }
+
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PLAY:
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PAUSE:
             case KeyEvent.KEYCODE_MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE:
@@ -5234,6 +5288,28 @@ public class PhoneWindowManager implements WindowManagerPolicy {
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * GPD XD+ (§105): is an HDMI cable/monitor attached?
+     *
+     * The Mapper-button recovery only exists to repair a mirror-induced display
+     * freeze, so with nothing plugged in the button must stay a no-op rather than
+     * sleeping the device on a stray press. The extcon switch reports HPD, and it
+     * still reads 1 while the pipeline is frozen, which is exactly when the button
+     * is needed.
+     *
+     * Fails OPEN: if the node cannot be read, allow the recovery. Losing the only
+     * recovery from a frozen screen is far worse than an occasional stray bounce.
+     */
+    private boolean isXdplusHdmiCablePresent() {
+        try (FileReader in = new FileReader("/sys/class/switch/hdmi/state")) {
+            final int c = in.read();
+            return c != '0';
+        } catch (Exception e) {
+            Slog.w(TAG, "XD+ recovery key: cannot read HDMI switch state, allowing", e);
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+
     private void wakeUpFromPowerKey(long eventTime) {
         wakeUp(eventTime, mAllowTheaterModeWakeFromPowerKey,
                 PowerManager.WAKE_REASON_POWER_BUTTON, "android.policy:POWER");
-- 
2.55.0

